row data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle mathcolor=\"black\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mstyle></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle mathcolor=\"red\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mstyle></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\">]</mo></mrow></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> is <em>not</em> a rotation-scaling matrix since the entries on the main diagonal are not the same.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>In conclusion, the correct answer is \"None.\"</p>\n</div></div>",
