    "q-140397": {
      "dom_id": "step-q140397",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14243854/assets/951fe7ccfd52e5f5c1b35a6e4cad4a626ed81c64e58adc26c971c654fac3b041.png)\n\nThe vectors $v$ and $Av$ are shown above. If $A$ is a rotation-scaling matrix, then $A=$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $A$ is a rotation-scaling matrix, then we can write\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}r & 0 \\\\ 0 & r\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the scale factor and $\\theta $ is the angle of rotation. \n\nAccording to the diagram, $r=4$ and $\\theta =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}r & 0 \\\\ 0 & r\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{2} & -2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} & -2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
