    "q-81653": {
      "dom_id": "step-q81653",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14243854/assets/360b780f8acf02d79da6c944612e250ac5b3c1d1916dfd0ed164b845bd83444d.png)\n\nThe vectors $v$ and $Av$ are shown above. If $A$ is a rotation-scaling matrix, then $A=$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $A$ is a rotation-scaling matrix, then we can write\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}r & 0 \\\\ 0 & r\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the scale factor and $\\theta $ is the angle of rotation. \n\nAccording to the diagram, $r=3$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}r & 0 \\\\ 0 & r\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-81653-a",
              "type": "math",
