    "q-39368": {
      "dom_id": "step-q39368",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Find the scale factor of the transformation represented by the rotation-scaling matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & -2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{3} & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "The scale factor $r$ of the rotation-scaling matrix $[\\begin{aligned}a & -b \\\\ b & a\\end{aligned}]$ can be found using the formula \n\n$$\nr=\\sqrt{det(A)}=\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{det(A)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+{(2\\sqrt{3})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}+12} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
