    "q-38506": {
      "dom_id": "step-q38506",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Find the scale factor of the transformation represented by the rotation-scaling matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & -2 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "The scale factor $r$ of the rotation-scaling matrix $[\\begin{aligned}a & -b \\\\ b & a\\end{aligned}]$ can be found using the formula \n\n$$\nr=\\sqrt{det(A)}=\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{det(A)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{5})^{2}+(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
