      "source_example_id": "e-2181",
      "knowledge_point": "Sketching the Image of a Vector Under the Action Of a Rotation-Scaling Matrix",
      "kp_id": "e-2181"
    },
    "q-81702": {
      "dom_id": "step-q81702",
      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14243854/assets/cb5c201068966a7d25ff3640d478e03a78bc075900181bdee93d5612b0217609.png)\n\nConsider the vector $v$ shown above. Find the vector $Av$ given that \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that $A$ is a rotation-scaling matrix. So, we need to find its scale factor and the angle of rotation.\n\nWe can find the scale factor using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{det(A)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(0)}^{2}+{(3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent $A$ as a product of a rotation and a scaling matrix, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =3[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}r & 0 \\\\ 0 & r\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =1\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, in order to find $Av$, we need to rotate $v$ counterclockwise by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$  and scale the result by a scale factor of $3,$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14243854/assets/7165c52d2280e4a53dc640acdca7671dcb897921028e675a583c46e6ccd40e33.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
